The test data of SwiftStreets, and its terms. Files ending in `.lzma` are
LZMA (xz) compressed, as Foundation's `NSData.compressed(using: .lzma)`
writes them. Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0
(https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright).

osm2streets/
    The 29 XML test cases of osm2streets (https://github.com/a-b-street/osm2streets,
    revision fc119c4, tests/src/): `input.osm`, `boundary.json`, `test.json`
    and the committed `geometry.json` of each, unchanged but compressed.
    osm2streets is under the Apache License 2.0 (the `LICENSE` beside them).
    The OSM extracts in them are (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0.
    The case `frederiksted` (PBF input) is left out: the port reads XML only.

moscow/
    OpenStreetMap extracts of central Moscow, fetched from Overpass on
    2026-10-23 and 2026-10-24 for five z15 tiles (15/19808/10242,
    15/19809/10242, 15/19808/10243, 15/19809/10243, 15/19810/10243: each
    tile and a 100 m margin) and for the 2x2 block of the first four (their data merged),
    written as OSM XML by `Parity/OverpassXML.swift`. The block's
    `boundary.json` is the clip its roads were reconstructed with.
    (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0.

rust/
    The results of the Rust osm2streets-cli (osm2streets fc119c4, see
    Docs/PortingParity.md) on the inputs above and on the synthetic ways of
    `Parity/SyntheticWays.swift`, stored as digests by `FreezeOracle`. They
    are derived from the OSM data above: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0.

earcutr/
    The fixtures (`tests/fixtures/`) and the recorded test outputs
    (`viz/testoutput/`) of the earcutr 0.4.3 crate
    (https://github.com/frewsxcv/earcutr), under the ISC License (the
    `LICENSE` beside them).

country-boundaries/
    The boundary rasters of the country-boundaries 1.2.0 crate
    (https://github.com/westnordost/country-boundaries-rust): the code is
    under the Apache License 2.0 (the `LICENSE` beside them), the data is
    derived from OpenStreetMap, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0.
